decision to make a clean Windows machine work without a manual SDK install. It
is not a legal conclusion, and this paragraph must not be cited as one.

If that review happens and comes back negative, the fix is already designed to
be cheap: the bundled adb is the **lowest** priority candidate in the
resolution order (`configured -> RIVIU_ADB_PATH -> ANDROID_SDK_ROOT ->
ANDROID_HOME -> PATH -> bundled`), so deleting these four files removes the
exposure and leaves every machine that has its own adb working exactly as
before.


