4. pymobiledevice3 and tidevice — frozen into the iOS sidecar
-------------------------------------------------------------

The Windows installer ships `riviu-pmd.exe`, a PyInstaller onefile build of
`sidecars/pymobiledevice3/riviu_pmd.py`. That executable **embeds** the
following, pinned in `sidecars/pymobiledevice3/requirements.txt` and locked by
`requirements-lock.txt`:

    pymobiledevice3 == 10.1.0    https://github.com/doronz88/pymobiledevice3
    tidevice        == 0.12.11   https://github.com/alibaba/taobao-iphone-device

plus their transitive dependencies, and the CPython runtime itself. Each
carries its own licence, reproduced by those projects; freezing them into one
executable does not change any of them, and the aggregate is not MIT.

Apple's usbmux (`AppleMobileDeviceProcess.exe`, Microsoft Store package
`AppleInc.AppleDevices`) is a **prerequisite installed separately by the
operator**. It is deliberately not redistributed, and nothing in this project
bundles it.


5. yt-dlp — Unlicense (public domain dedication)
------------------------------------------------

    yt-dlp    https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp

Shipped beside the app so the desktop can ask TikTok what a post says and what
pictures it has, without driving a phone to find out. `crates/core/src/
tiktok_web.rs` is the only caller; `sidecars/yt-dlp/README.md` says why an
extractor is needed for what looks like one HTTP request.

yt-dlp is released into the public domain under the Unlicense, which imposes no
attribution requirement. It is listed here anyway, because this file is a record
of what ships and not only of what must be credited.

**Not committed to this repository, and deliberately not pinned by hash.** The
binary is fetched per machine and per release build. TikTok breaks extractors on
its own schedule and the fix is always a newer yt-dlp, so a pinned copy would be
a pinned failure. `RIVIU_YTDLP_PATH` points a run at any other copy. With no
yt-dlp present, every lookup fails as `NoBinary` and the product behaves as it
did before the sidecar existed.

yt-dlp bundles its own dependencies in the published `.exe`, each under its own
licence. Freezing them into one executable does not change any of them.


6. What is missing from this repository
---------------------------------------

There is no `LICENSE` file at the repository root. `Cargo.toml` says `MIT`, so
the intent exists, but the text it refers to does not. Shipping other people's
code while your own licence is a single word in a manifest is the worst of both
positions, and adding that file is recommended — it is a decision for whoever
owns this project, not something this NOTICE can settle.
